@prefix chg: <https://semblance.dev/ns/change#> .
@prefix mig: <https://semblance.dev/ns/migration#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix change: <https://semblance.dev/change/> .
@prefix c: <https://semblance.dev/ns/component#> .
@prefix sem: <https://semblance.dev/ns/core#> .

# What changed for whoever has to move with it: AGENTS.md, "When a component changes".

change:charts-on-shared-parts a chg:Change ;
    rdfs:label "The bar chart, heatmap and line chart are series charts, drawn from the shared chart parts"@en ;
    chg:issue <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/384> ;
    chg:motivation """Each of the three charts had a rule of its own that read the view's rows and repeated the series
sub-select four times, re-rendered the whole chart on any changed row, wrote its numbers in en-US, and (the line
chart, an SVG) did not mirror right to left. The series charts already had shared parts for all of this: a plan
that mints series, categories and points, a layout that adds scales and neighbours, a legend that toggles series,
points placed by custom properties. The three now use them, so a changed row re-renders its marks and a new kind
is mostly its marks.""" ;
    chg:substance """c:BarChart and c:Heatmap are c:SeriesChart kinds, c:LineChart a c:AxisChart kind. What a consumer
states about them (c:view, c:categoryVariable, c:seriesVariable, c:valueVariable, c:facetVariable, c:facetLabel,
c:legend, c:unit, c:emptyText, c:flagVariable, c:flagLabel, c:logScale, c:referenceLine) means what it meant;
no term went.

c:SeriesPlan learned what the three need, each said by the kind: facets (c:faceted: a c:ChartFacet per value of
c:facetVariable in the order first seen, and a facet's own categories and points, c:facet), category components
(c:categoryClass, with c:total and c:measured) and points placed in them (c:pointsIn "category"), a point for
every series and category of a facet (c:fullGrid, with c:flagged), points for values above zero only
(c:positiveValues), and numeric categories on an x scale (c:numericCategories, c:xAt). c:SeriesLayout adds a
facet's longest bar (c:max on the facet), log scales in decades (c:logValues; the x scale with c:logScale; a tick's
c:value its power of ten), the next point of a numeric series by x (c:nextX) and the linear reference
(c:refX1, c:refY1, c:refX2, c:refY2). A kind with c:minCategories shows its c:emptyText, else "Needs at least two
sizes.", with fewer numeric categories. A kind with c:saysRows keeps c:RowChartText, a line per row, as its Text
modality (the bar chart and heatmap); the line chart's Text modality is now its points' words (c:SeriesChartText).

What renders differently:
- Bar chart: a bar is a c:BarCategory component (div.sem-bar: span.sem-category, ol.sem-track, span.sem-total), a
  segment a c:BarPoint (li.sem-point.sem-bar-point holding span.sem-seg, its words visually hidden, a tab stop in
  the chart's arrow-key navigation), as wide as --v of its figure's --max. Totals and words are in the viewer's
  locale with up to two decimals ("1,200.5 €", not "1201 €"); "running…" is c:ChartRunningPhrase in the viewer's
  language. The legend is the shared one (toggle buttons; hidden with one series); a segment's value is the sum of
  its rows' values times their multiplicity (it was the first row's).
- Heatmap: a cell is a c:HeatCell (td.sem-point, with sem-h0 to sem-h12, sem-flagged or sem-pending), its digits in
  the viewer's locale; a row's heading is the series' legend label (it was its key); rows are in the series' order
  across facets (they were in the order first seen within each facet); an unfaceted heatmap has no empty caption.
- Line chart: no SVG. It is an axis chart (figure with the plot, ticks, marks, x ticks below, the shared legend),
  its y ticks decades (unit-less), its x ticks a nice scale (decades with c:logScale) rather than each size, a point a
  c:LinePoint (li.sem-point.sem-line-point with a dot and the segment to the next), the reference a
  span.sem-reference and its word span.sem-reference-label. One series has no legend.""" ;
    chg:forwardGuide """Nothing to move in the graph. A stylesheet or test that read the old markup: the bar chart's
.sem-seg is now inside li.sem-bar-point and carries the series color (background: var(--color)); the heatmap's td
has class sem-point before its ramp class; the line chart's svg, .sem-grid, .sem-axis, .sem-line and .sem-dot
(the SVG circle) are gone, its marks are .sem-chart-marks > .sem-point as in the other axis charts. A test that
compared a bar chart's total or tooltip text compares the viewer's locale's, at most two decimals.""" ;
    chg:backwardGuide """Nothing to move in the graph either way: the terms the kinds read are those they read before,
and the new ones are derived or said by the framework's own classes. Going back returns the old markup and its
en-US numbers.""" ;
    chg:affects c:BarChart , c:Heatmap , c:LineChart , c:RowChart , c:SeriesChart , c:AxisChart , c:ChartPoint , c:AreaPoint .
